      "question": "Based on the FY2024 filings, compare the primary strategic objectives of AEP and ED.",
      "expected_answer": "AEP's filing does not explicitly state a strategic objective in the provided excerpts; it lists risk factors. ED's filing states: 'Con Edison seeks to provide shareholder value through continued dividend growth, supported by earnings growth in regulated utilities and electric transmission projects.' Thus, ED has a clear shareholder-focused strategy, while AEP's excerpt concentrates on forward-looking statements and risks.",
      "predicted_answer": "**Conclusion:** ED explicitly states a primary strategic objective in Item 7; the supplied AEP Item 7 evidence does not explicitly state a strategic objective.\n\n- **ED (FY2024):** \"Con Edison seeks to provide shareholder value through continued dividend growth, supported by earnings growth in regulated utilities and electric transmission projects\" [E2].\n- **AEP (FY2024):** No explicit strategic objective appears in the retrieved Item 7 text; the excerpt contains only an incorporation-by-reference statement and forward-looking risk factors [E1][E3][E5].\n\n**Comparison:** ED's objective is stated as shareholder value via dividend growth backed by regulated utility and transmission earnings growth [E2], while AEP's Item 7 excerpt discloses no explicitly framed primary objective [E1][E3][E5]. This is an asymmetry in the supplied evidence, not proof that AEP's filing lacks one.\n\nSources:\n[E1] AEP_2024.html — Item 7\n[E2] ED_2024.html — Item 7\n[E3] AEP_2024.html — Item 7\n[E5] AEP_2024.html — Item 7",
