      "task_type": "cross-company-year-hybrid",
      "question": "In their Item 7 MD&A, which company explicitly states that they provide quantitative information about the impact of changes in volume and pricing on sales, and at which organizational level do they report this? Provide textual evidence from both ECL's FY2022 and LIN's FY2024 filings, and identify which financial table or note is referenced for additional segment detail.",
      "expected_answer": "ECL's FY2022 Item 7 states: 'We provide quantitative information about the material sales drivers including the impact of changes in volume and pricing and the effect of acquisitions and changes in foreign currency at the corporate and reportable segment level.' LIN's FY2024 Item 7 does not contain a similar explicit statement; instead it directs readers to 'Note 18 to the consolidated financial statements for additional information related to Linde’s reportable segments.' This Note 18 constitutes the financial table referenced for segment details.",
      "predicted_answer": "**Conclusion:** ECL explicitly states it provides quantitative volume/pricing sales-driver information; LIN does not make that statement but presents the data.\n\n**ECL — FY2022, Item 7**\n\"We provide quantitative information about the material sales drivers including the impact of changes in volume and pricing and the effect of acquisitions and changes in foreign currency at the corporate and reportable segment level.\" [E1] ECL references \"the consolidated financial statements and related notes included in this Form 10-K\" for segment detail, but the ledger does not include a specific note number. [E1]\n\n**LIN — FY2024, Item 7**\nNo equivalent explicit statement appears; LIN instead presents \"Factors Contributing to Changes - Sales\" tables (Volume, Price/Mix, Cost pass-through, Currency, Acquisitions/Divestitures) for the Americas, EMEA, APAC, Engineering, and Other segments. [E2][E4][E5][E10] The segment note reference to Note 18 appears in Item 1, not Item 7. [E3]\n\n**Comparison:** Only ECL explicitly states the disclosure; it reports at the corporate and reportable segment level. [E1] LIN shows the same drivers by reportable segment without that statement. [E2]\n\nSources\n[E1] ECL_2022.html — Item 7, MD&A\n[E2] LIN_2024.html — Item 7, MD&A\n[E3] LIN_2024.html — Item 1, Business\n[E4] LIN_2024.html — Item 7, MD&A\n[E5] LIN_2024.html — Item 7, MD&A\n[E10] LIN_2024.html — Item 7, MD&A",
